## Why This Is Asked

Explores cost trade-offs of on-device privacy-preserving telemetry at scale, balancing data minimization with operational transparency.

## Key Concepts

- On-device aggregation and secure aggregation
- Data minimization vs. data utility
- Compliance costs vs. backend savings
- Phased rollout and break-even metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: merge deltas with secure aggregation placeholder
function aggregateDeltas(deltas, state) {
  // secure-aggregate-friendly merge
  const merged = deltas.reduce((acc, d) => acc + d.value, 0);
  state.total += merged;
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you model drift and re-authorization costs if consent preferences change?
- What latency/throughput targets would you set for real-time dashboards under offline conditions?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess the candidate’s ability to structure a practical CBA for a distributed architecture shift, weighing latency, privacy, and cost against risk reduction and retention gains.

## Key Concepts
- Edge computing vs centralized analytics
- Inference costs, device storage, data transfer
- Regulatory/compliance penalties and risk
- Uplift in fraud detection and user retention
- Break-even analysis and sensitivity testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function breakEven(initialCost, monthlySavings, monthlyCosts) {
  let months = 0;
  let net = -initialCost;
  while (net < 0) {
    net += (monthlySavings - monthlyCosts);
    months++;
  }
  return months;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design the data governance model to satisfy privacy regulations across regions?
- What mitigation plans exist if edge devices underperform (false positives, latency spikes, battery impact)?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to translate connectivity challenges into a minimal, privacy-conscious on-device flow with cost trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Edge batching, offline queues, deduping
- Energy/memory budgeting, latency impact
- Privacy, consent, rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function batchRequests(requests, maxBatch) {
  const batches = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < requests.length; i += maxBatch) {
    batches.push(requests.slice(i, i + maxBatch));
  }
  return batches;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle failed batches in poor connectivity differently for iOS vs Android?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate break-even without compromising privacy?

## Why This Is Asked

Explore data-locality, privacy, and practical CBA modeling for a lightweight client-side feature in a cloud data platform.

## Key Concepts

- Data locality and offline caching
- Cost modeling: storage, compute, network
- Privacy/compliance: anonymization, retention, audits
